  "variants": {"direct":{"input":{"url":"https://math.example.org/math-temml-aligned","title":"Math temml aligned equations","description":"Math temml aligned equations: a short note used as a test page.","hasPublishedOrAuthor":true,"options":{},"smallImages":[],"mainPath":[2,3,3],"variant":"direct"},"steps":{"footnotes":null,"callouts":null,"standardize":"<article> <p>The proof begins with a simple observation about the shape of the curve, which the author states without ceremony and then spends three pages defending against every obvious objection.</p> <p>What follows is the usual machinery, assembled with care, and the reader who has followed this far will recognise each step before it is taken, though perhaps not the order in which they are arranged.</p> <p>The result, when it arrives, is smaller than the build-up suggests, and the author says as much, which is part of why the paper is still read.</p><p>Matrix <math data-latex=\"1234\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd> <mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr> <mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd> <mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> as before.</p><p>Cases <math data-latex=\"{xif x>0-xotherwise\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>{</mo> <mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd> <mtd><mtext>if </mtext> <mi>x</mi> <mo>&gt;</mo> <mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr> <mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo> <mi>x</mi></mtd> <mtd><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></math> as before.</p><p>Aligned <math data-latex=\"a=b+1c=d\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd> <mtd><mo>=</mo> <mi>b</mi> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr> <mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd> <mtd><mo>=</mo> <mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math> as before.</p><p>Roots and fractions <math data-latex=\"-b±b2-4ac2a\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo> <mi>b</mi> <mo>±</mo> <msqrt><msup><mi>b</mi> <mn>2</mn></msup> <mo>-</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mi>a</mi> <mi>c</mi></msqrt></mrow> <mrow><mn>2</mn> <mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> as before.</p><p>Cube root <math data-latex=\"x3\" display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mroot><mi>x</mi> <mn>3</mn></mroot></math> as before.</p><p>Scripts <math data-latex=\"xi2+yjk\" display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>x</mi> <mi>i</mi> <mn>2</mn></msubsup> <mo>+</mo> <msub><mi>y</mi> <mrow><mi>j</mi> <mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></math> as before.</p><p>Sum <math data-latex=\"∑i=1ni2\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>∑</mo> <mrow><mi>i</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn></mrow> <mi>n</mi></munderover> <msup><mi>i</mi> <mn>2</mn></msup></math> as before.</p><p>Tensor <math data-latex=\"Tabc\" display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>T</mi> <mi>a</mi> <mi>b</mi> <mi>c</mi></mmultiscripts></math> as before.</p><p>Bars <math data-latex=\"|x+y|≤‖x‖+‖y‖\" display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>+</mo> <mi>y</mi> <mo>|</mo> <mo>≤</mo> <mo>‖</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>‖</mo> <mo>+</mo> <mo>‖</mo> <mi>y</mi> <mo>‖</mo></math> as before.</p><p>Parentheses <math data-latex=\"(a+[b])(c\" display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi> <mo>+</mo> <mo>[</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo> <mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi></math> as before.</p><p>Enclosure <math data-latex=\"E=mc2\" display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"box\"><mi>E</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mi>m</mi> <msup><mi>c</mi> <mn>2</mn></msup></menclose></math> as before.</p><p>Fraction rules <math data-latex=\"nk,12\" display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mi>n</mi> <mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> as before.</p><p>The result, when it arrives, is smaller than the build-up suggests, and the author says as much, which is part of why the paper is still read.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <math data-latex=\"\\begin{align}a&=b\\tag{1}\\\\c&=d\\label{eq:c}\\end{align}\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd> <mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo> <mi>b</mi></mrow></mtd> <mtd><mtext>(1)</mtext></mtd></mtr> <mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd> <mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo> <mi>d</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math> as before.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <math data-latex=\"\\begin{aligned}x&=1\\\\y&=2\\end{aligned}\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd> <mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr> <mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd> <mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math> as before.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <math data-latex=\"\\begin{gather*}a\\\\b\\end{gather*}\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd></mtr> <mtr><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math> as before.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <math data-latex=\"\\begin{multline}a+b\\\\+c+d\\end{multline}\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>a</mi> <mo>+</mo> <mi>b</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr> <mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">+</mo> <mi>c</mi> <mo>+</mo> <mi>d</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math> as before.</p><p>Consider the following expression: <math data-latex=\"\\begin{alignat}{2}a&=b&c&=d\\\\e&=f&g&=h\\end{alignat}\" display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd> <mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo> <mi>b</mi></mrow></mtd> <mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd> <mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo> <mi>d</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr> <mtr>